<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thirty-five Years in the East</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thirty-five Years in the East is a memoir by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-martin-honigberger">Johann Martin Honigberger</a>, a European physician who served at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a>. It describes his travels and experiences in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> and neighbouring regions. Accounts of the Sikh Empire name it, with the correspondence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-francois-allard">Jean-François Allard</a>, among the memoirs of European officers and servants of the Lahore Darbar that are important primary sources.</p></div>
